  "title": "Journal v2: schema-validated, indexed run journals",
  "summary": "The journal module is split into five files and grows from a two-payload buffer into a versioned, schema-validated event log. Events now carry an actor (harness/person/system), an optional work item and change, and an optional cost; eight payload types replace the original two. Every appended event is validated against a draft 2020-12 JSON schema before a byte is written, and a run-complete event must name the journal's current head hash. Journals move from `<state_dir>/buffer/<run>.jsonl` to `<state_dir>/runs/<run>.jsonl`, run ids are validated as safe single path components, and the first accepted event records the run in a per-work-item index under `<state_dir>/index`. A new reader replays a journal, checking schema, chain links and run-complete placement, and returns no events at all when any line fails.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
